WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:03.820
- Today I am not in Germany with BMW

00:00:03.820 --> 00:00:05.670
at their Next Gen Event for the launch

00:00:05.670 --> 00:00:08.580
of the BMW IX, as we
had originally planned.

00:00:08.580 --> 00:00:13.370
So instead, they sent
the car to me, sort of.

00:00:13.370 --> 00:00:15.210
This is the most unique
way to do a car launch.

00:00:15.210 --> 00:00:16.520
I mean, we're seeing it here,

00:00:16.520 --> 00:00:18.860
before anybody else
actually gets to see it,

00:00:18.860 --> 00:00:20.380
and then we're gonna 3D print it,

00:00:20.380 --> 00:00:23.110
and see it in real life,
but in the palm of my hands.

00:00:23.110 --> 00:00:24.700
I went to CES with BMW this year,

00:00:24.700 --> 00:00:26.260
and I had the best time ever,

00:00:26.260 --> 00:00:28.170
and we talked about how
much fun we were gonna have,

00:00:28.170 --> 00:00:30.200
when I would come out
to Germany this year.

00:00:30.200 --> 00:00:32.860
And unfortunately, because
pretty much the whole world

00:00:32.860 --> 00:00:35.430
has shut down, and all of
the travel restrictions,

00:00:35.430 --> 00:00:36.640
I wasn't able to make it out.

00:00:36.640 --> 00:00:38.040
But they still wanted me to feel

00:00:38.040 --> 00:00:39.530
like I was a part of the launch,

00:00:39.530 --> 00:00:42.230
and to be able to bring you
guys along for the ride,

00:00:42.230 --> 00:00:43.400
all puns intended.

00:00:43.400 --> 00:00:45.220
So since the car was being launched today,

00:00:45.220 --> 00:00:48.470
they wanted me to be able to see the car,

00:00:48.470 --> 00:00:49.930
feel the car, touch the car,

00:00:49.930 --> 00:00:52.580
but obviously they couldn't
send the actual car here.

00:00:52.580 --> 00:00:55.890
But what they did send was a 3D printer,

00:00:55.890 --> 00:00:59.670
all of the accessories, the
materials, and a 3D file

00:00:59.670 --> 00:01:02.160
to print out a tiny replica

00:01:02.160 --> 00:01:04.200
so I could actually see
the thing for myself.

00:01:04.200 --> 00:01:06.660
They're calling this "The Tiny Launch"!

00:01:06.660 --> 00:01:09.020
Like a tiny launch, it's
like the cutest thing

00:01:09.020 --> 00:01:09.853
I've ever heard!

00:01:09.853 --> 00:01:11.360
So what's even more fun is the fact

00:01:11.360 --> 00:01:13.770
that I got to watch this thing be printed.

00:01:13.770 --> 00:01:16.100
I've never printed anything
before in my entire life

00:01:16.100 --> 00:01:17.560
by myself in 3D.

00:01:17.560 --> 00:01:19.950
So the fact that this was my first print,

00:01:19.950 --> 00:01:23.990
an unreleased, never before
seen, brand new, BMW IX,

00:01:23.990 --> 00:01:26.360
this vehicle design marks the beginning

00:01:26.360 --> 00:01:28.300
of an all new era for electric vehicles.

00:01:28.300 --> 00:01:31.110
So my friends, let's
take to the 3D printer,

00:01:31.110 --> 00:01:32.307
and print ourselves a car.

00:01:32.307 --> 00:01:33.760
Now before we get into
this, let me just tell you

00:01:33.760 --> 00:01:35.780
that 3D printing takes a very long time.

00:01:35.780 --> 00:01:37.440
I think this total project

00:01:37.440 --> 00:01:40.474
probably took over two
days of just print time.

00:01:40.474 --> 00:01:43.057
(techno music)

00:01:45.370 --> 00:01:46.500
We have the model in place.

00:01:46.500 --> 00:01:47.720
Everything is ready to go.

00:01:47.720 --> 00:01:48.860
We're gonna do a time lapse.

00:01:48.860 --> 00:01:49.981
Are you guys ready?

00:01:49.981 --> 00:01:51.420
(techno music)

00:01:51.420 --> 00:01:54.820
So right now it's sending
the car to the printer.

00:01:54.820 --> 00:01:57.870
And this actual printing
process took several days,

00:01:57.870 --> 00:02:00.820
from the shell, to the
rims, to the outer tires.

00:02:00.820 --> 00:02:02.660
And this type if printing
process that we did

00:02:02.660 --> 00:02:04.510
was actually a very different process

00:02:04.510 --> 00:02:06.000
than I've ever seen before.

00:02:06.000 --> 00:02:07.800
It uses liquid resin,
which is then released

00:02:07.800 --> 00:02:09.270
inside of this tank.

00:02:09.270 --> 00:02:13.710
And very precise lasers will
etch this resin and harden it,

00:02:13.710 --> 00:02:16.404
so it's basically being
built from the bottom up.

00:02:16.404 --> 00:02:18.987
(techno music)

00:02:22.780 --> 00:02:24.873
The print is finished.

00:02:26.360 --> 00:02:28.633
26 hours later.

00:02:29.720 --> 00:02:31.650
And then you take it out,
and then you put it in

00:02:31.650 --> 00:02:33.990
a very high concentrate of alcohol.

00:02:33.990 --> 00:02:35.660
You give it a little bath.

00:02:35.660 --> 00:02:37.290
This is so cool!

00:02:37.290 --> 00:02:39.570
I wish that I was in Germany
right now for the launch,

00:02:39.570 --> 00:02:43.480
but I guess this is the next best thing!

00:02:43.480 --> 00:02:46.620
I just saw that they're
calling this a tiny launch.

00:02:46.620 --> 00:02:48.293
It's a tiny launch!

00:02:48.293 --> 00:02:50.876
(techno music)

00:02:52.242 --> 00:02:53.217
You guys think 3D printing is easy,

00:02:53.217 --> 00:02:54.740
you think it's like an easy thing?

00:02:54.740 --> 00:02:56.340
You think it's just like, you know,

00:02:56.340 --> 00:02:58.790
you push print and then you're done?

00:02:58.790 --> 00:03:00.660
Spoiler alert, you want
a high quality print,

00:03:00.660 --> 00:03:01.922
that's not the case.

00:03:01.922 --> 00:03:04.505
(techno music)

00:03:08.072 --> 00:03:09.350
So now I need to clean this up,

00:03:09.350 --> 00:03:11.141
get it in the curing oven.

00:03:11.141 --> 00:03:13.724
(techno music)

00:03:30.424 --> 00:03:31.360
Oh, you're wondering why it's dark?

00:03:31.360 --> 00:03:35.481
Maybe because this process
has taken a very long time.

00:03:35.481 --> 00:03:37.731
(spraying)

00:03:39.990 --> 00:03:40.990
I think I did it.

00:03:40.990 --> 00:03:44.810
So now, I guess we wait for this to dry.

00:03:44.810 --> 00:03:46.870
Repeat the same process for the wheels.

00:03:46.870 --> 00:03:49.052
I love my new hobby.

00:03:49.052 --> 00:03:51.635
(techno music)

00:03:56.683 --> 00:03:59.743
I mean, it's almost like being in Germany.

00:04:00.680 --> 00:04:03.267
It's so, it's so lifelike (chuckles).

00:04:04.610 --> 00:04:06.010
Can you imagine me?

00:04:06.010 --> 00:04:06.843
This is me.

00:04:08.860 --> 00:04:11.393
Okay, so my wheel fell off
(wheel snaps in place).

00:04:11.393 --> 00:04:13.910
(beep) I am so, just impressed,

00:04:13.910 --> 00:04:15.970
the fact that I did not
mess up my first print,

00:04:15.970 --> 00:04:17.340
and I am very grateful that I didn't

00:04:17.340 --> 00:04:19.250
because we didn't have enough time

00:04:19.250 --> 00:04:20.410
to be able to print another one,

00:04:20.410 --> 00:04:22.570
and get this video up
for you guys (chuckling).

00:04:22.570 --> 00:04:24.650
So a vehicle like this
usually has a lead time

00:04:24.650 --> 00:04:25.483
of several years.

00:04:25.483 --> 00:04:28.360
But today, BMW is showcasing
their first model.

00:04:28.360 --> 00:04:29.550
And it's pretty cool that
we're actually getting

00:04:29.550 --> 00:04:33.010
to take a look at this
thing before it's even out.

00:04:33.010 --> 00:04:35.180
I am very sad though, that
I'm not actually there

00:04:35.180 --> 00:04:37.300
in person to get to see it, to sit in it,

00:04:37.300 --> 00:04:39.160
and to just sort of feel what it's like

00:04:39.160 --> 00:04:40.330
to actually be in this car.

00:04:40.330 --> 00:04:42.120
But I feel so grateful

00:04:42.120 --> 00:04:43.860
that I'm still able to
participate in the fun

00:04:43.860 --> 00:04:46.040
by getting to print one of
these for you guys to see.

00:04:46.040 --> 00:04:48.960
While this very spacious, cozy interior

00:04:48.960 --> 00:04:51.050
might look like a place
that you can relax,

00:04:51.050 --> 00:04:55.980
this car can go from
zero to 100 real quick,

00:04:55.980 --> 00:04:57.320
in about five seconds.

00:04:57.320 --> 00:04:59.840
It has two electric motors
that have maximum output

00:04:59.840 --> 00:05:01.420
of more than 500 horsepower.

00:05:01.420 --> 00:05:03.230
It also has DC fast charging,

00:05:03.230 --> 00:05:04.730
so you can charge the battery

00:05:04.730 --> 00:05:07.890
from 10 to 80% of its full
capacity in 40 minutes.

00:05:07.890 --> 00:05:10.350
A 10 minute fast charge will add 75 miles

00:05:10.350 --> 00:05:11.280
to the car's range.

00:05:11.280 --> 00:05:13.250
I love BMW's focus on sustainability,

00:05:13.250 --> 00:05:15.210
and this car is no exception.

00:05:15.210 --> 00:05:17.250
The power used to produce
the battery cells,

00:05:17.250 --> 00:05:20.130
the high voltage battery and
the entire vehicle itself

00:05:20.130 --> 00:05:22.410
comes exclusively from renewable sources.

00:05:22.410 --> 00:05:24.870
There's a high proportion of
recycled and natural materials

00:05:24.870 --> 00:05:27.290
that were used for the
exterior and the interior,

00:05:27.290 --> 00:05:30.090
and the leather is tanned
with olive leaf extracts.

00:05:30.090 --> 00:05:31.740
I talked a lot about the sustainability

00:05:31.740 --> 00:05:34.600
that BMW has been doing in
my video that I did at CES,

00:05:34.600 --> 00:05:36.700
so it's really cool to see
them sort of follow through

00:05:36.700 --> 00:05:38.320
with all of that in this one as well.

00:05:38.320 --> 00:05:40.980
The new intelligence panel
has integrated sensors,

00:05:40.980 --> 00:05:42.730
a camera, and radar technology

00:05:42.730 --> 00:05:44.070
for advanced driver assistance.

00:05:44.070 --> 00:05:46.230
This is bringing together
the latest innovation

00:05:46.230 --> 00:05:47.860
in the fields of electric mobility,

00:05:47.860 --> 00:05:50.210
automated driving, and
intelligent connectivity.

00:05:50.210 --> 00:05:51.400
5G, my friends!

00:05:51.400 --> 00:05:53.740
The future of 5G is just gonna give us

00:05:53.740 --> 00:05:55.450
so many more opportunities,

00:05:55.450 --> 00:05:57.720
and this is 5G enabled, so it'll allow

00:05:57.720 --> 00:06:00.780
for optimized automated
driving and parking functions.

00:06:00.780 --> 00:06:02.960
Now the doors have frameless windows.

00:06:02.960 --> 00:06:05.330
The tailgate has no separation joints,

00:06:05.330 --> 00:06:07.700
and this extends across
the entire back of the car.

00:06:07.700 --> 00:06:09.760
These new design changes are allowing

00:06:09.760 --> 00:06:11.650
for increased efficiency and range

00:06:11.650 --> 00:06:14.280
with the intelligent, lightweight
design and aerodynamics.

00:06:14.280 --> 00:06:16.380
It's made of an aluminum
space frame construction,

00:06:16.380 --> 00:06:17.510
with carbon cage.

00:06:17.510 --> 00:06:20.880
Now this curved interior
display, we just needed,

00:06:20.880 --> 00:06:22.500
I'm just gonna, did you see that?

00:06:22.500 --> 00:06:23.860
Let me just back that video up for you,

00:06:23.860 --> 00:06:25.090
because we need to see it again.

00:06:25.090 --> 00:06:28.580
It's a fully digital screen,
made up of a 12.3 inch display

00:06:28.580 --> 00:06:30.950
and a 14.9 inch control display,

00:06:30.950 --> 00:06:33.220
and it's a single piece
of frameless glass.

00:06:33.220 --> 00:06:35.940
And I just cannot stop
looking at this image of it.

00:06:35.940 --> 00:06:39.550
And I've just been replaying
this video clip over and over.

00:06:39.550 --> 00:06:41.330
I also really like these seats.

00:06:41.330 --> 00:06:43.580
These are also newly
developed with this new style

00:06:43.580 --> 00:06:44.520
of head restraint.

00:06:44.520 --> 00:06:46.530
There's extra legroom, and there's space

00:06:46.530 --> 00:06:47.630
for storage compartments.

00:06:47.630 --> 00:06:50.240
Plus the center console kind of looks like

00:06:50.240 --> 00:06:52.100
a high quality piece of furniture.

00:06:52.100 --> 00:06:55.280
And this little dial, hold
on, let's replay the clip,

00:06:55.280 --> 00:06:57.830
it's like a diamond doorknob,

00:06:57.830 --> 00:06:59.870
something that I think everyone needs.

00:06:59.870 --> 00:07:02.380
Maybe not in their home, but in their car.

00:07:02.380 --> 00:07:03.570
We also need to take a moment

00:07:03.570 --> 00:07:05.210
to check out this steering wheel.

00:07:05.210 --> 00:07:06.930
It's hexagonal, which kind of gives it

00:07:06.930 --> 00:07:09.060
this really neat, futuristic look.

00:07:09.060 --> 00:07:13.000
And this panoramic glass
roof is also very impressive.

00:07:13.000 --> 00:07:15.000
It has the electro-chromic shading,

00:07:15.000 --> 00:07:17.170
which is available as an add-on option,

00:07:17.170 --> 00:07:19.060
and this is so cool, because
when you press a button,

00:07:19.060 --> 00:07:22.030
it'll basically turn
it into a tinted glass

00:07:22.030 --> 00:07:23.680
without having to do anything.

00:07:23.680 --> 00:07:25.310
It is magical.

00:07:25.310 --> 00:07:27.460
I am so excited for the
future of electric vehicles,

00:07:27.460 --> 00:07:29.170
and everything that car
manufacturers are doing

00:07:29.170 --> 00:07:31.180
to keep improving on this technology.

00:07:31.180 --> 00:07:32.760
And I've been loving everything

00:07:32.760 --> 00:07:34.240
that BMW has been showcasing,

00:07:34.240 --> 00:07:37.210
and I'm even more excited
to hopefully get a chance

00:07:37.210 --> 00:07:39.390
in the near future to
give this a test drive.

00:07:39.390 --> 00:07:41.890
Until then, I will see you
guys here on the Internet,

00:07:41.890 --> 00:07:44.130
and BMW, congrats on
another amazing launch,

00:07:44.130 --> 00:07:46.080
and thank you so much
for including me in this,

00:07:46.080 --> 00:07:48.050
even though I couldn't
join you guys in Germany,

00:07:48.050 --> 00:07:49.700
hopefully one of these days soon,

00:07:49.700 --> 00:07:52.373
I will see you guys
all again in real life.

00:07:52.373 --> 00:07:55.206
(slow jazz music)

00:07:57.554 --> 00:07:58.387
(beep)

00:07:58.387 --> 00:08:00.320
I'm trying to get you out here, bud.

00:08:00.320 --> 00:08:02.560
Hope I can get you out by the
time they launch this vehicle,

00:08:02.560 --> 00:08:05.763
'cause at this rate (sighs) I don't know.

